# tools/crypto_monocypher_poly1305_parity_witness.rish — Monocypher-source parity for the standalone Poly1305 one-time authenticator, the MAC that
# authenticates every sealed message. Our authored crypto/poly1305.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual), each
# compiled fresh and asked for the same eight tags, diffed byte-for-byte. The EIGHTH rung of the real Monocypher-source parity pattern (BLAKE2b ·
# X25519 · Ed25519 · IETF AEAD · Argon2 · XChaCha20-Poly1305 flagship · Edwards↔Montgomery came before). Season G · Cryptography.
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md — Season G's crux rungs name "the parity witness
# proving Rye output equals Monocypher output byte-for-byte." crypto/poly1305.rye's own selftest named Monocypher-source parity as an honest held
# horizon ("its vendored source is a held fetch"); this rung closes it. Poly1305 was proven inside the AEAD flagship, yet never STANDALONE against
# Monocypher's own crypto_poly1305 — so the MAC every Vault/Comlink/Lotus sealed carry rests on now stands proven in its own right.
# Kin: crypto/poly1305.rye (our authored authenticator, GREEN against Zig's std.crypto and the RFC vector) · tools/monocypher_poly1305_parity.rye (our
# printing harness) · tools/fixtures/monocypher_poly1305_harness.c (Monocypher's printing harness) · tools/crypto_monocypher_aead_parity_witness.rish
# (the AEAD sibling that exercised Poly1305 embedded, not standalone). Monocypher stays the parity TARGET, vendored and unmodified, never a copied line,
# studied clean-room (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# The eight lines are anchored to the world: the first seven are tags over deterministic messages of sizes {0, 1, 15, 16, 17, 34, 256} — the block
# edges the polynomial must cross (empty · sub-block · exact block · one byte over · the RFC's 34-byte length · a 256-byte multi-block run) — where the
# oracle is a second real implementation agreeing byte-for-byte; the eighth is the RFC 8439 §2.5.2 canonical message "Cryptographic Forum Research
# Group", whose published tag a8061dc1305136c6c22b8baf0c0127a9 anchors the parity to the standard. Every tag is under the RFC 8439 §2.5.2 one-time key.
# Purely local — no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_monocypher_poly1305_parity_witness.rish

say "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Language EN — Monocypher-source parity for the standalone Poly1305 one-time authenticator, the MAC that authenticates every sealed message. crypto/poly1305.rye named Monocypher-source parity as a held horizon and was only ever proven inside the AEAD flagship; this eighth rung closes the horizon and proves the authenticator STANDALONE against the ACTUAL vendored Monocypher C over eight tags, byte-for-byte."
say "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Style Radiant — like against like. Our authored authenticator and the unmodified vendored Monocypher each compile fresh and each print, in order, tags for deterministic messages of sizes {0, 1, 15, 16, 17, 34, 256} and then for the RFC 8439 §2.5.2 canonical message. Two independent implementations, one set of inputs; the parity is that the eight tags agree hex for hex."
say "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Lens TAME — no fabricated constant is trusted: the block-edge oracle is a second real implementation, and the eighth tag is anchored to RFC 8439 §2.5.2's published authenticator a8061dc1305136c6c22b8baf0c0127a9. The witness diffs the eight Monocypher lines against the eight Rye lines byte-for-byte AND asserts the published anchor. Monocypher is linked, never copied. Purely local — no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let cbin = "crypto/bin/monocypher_poly1305"
let cout = "crypto/bin/monocypher_poly1305.out"
let rout = "crypto/bin/rye_poly1305.out"

# 1. Build the Monocypher C harness, linking the unmodified vendored source with zig cc.
let cbuild = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && ${zig} cc -O2 -I vendor/monocypher/src tools/fixtures/monocypher_poly1305_harness.c vendor/monocypher/src/monocypher.c -o ${cbin}"]
assert cbuild.ok else "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Monocypher C harness build failed — ${cbuild.err}"

# 2. Run the Monocypher C harness — eight authenticator hex lines.
let crun = run ["sh" "-c" "${cbin} > ${cout} 2>&1"]
assert crun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Monocypher C harness exited non-zero — see ${cout}"

# 3. Run our authored Rye harness — eight authenticator hex lines over the identical inputs.
let rrun = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye run tools/monocypher_poly1305_parity.rye > ${rout} 2>&1"]
assert rrun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Rye harness exited non-zero — see ${rout}"

# 4. Byte-for-byte parity: the two eight-line outputs must be identical.
let diff = run ["sh" "-c" "diff ${cout} ${rout} > /dev/null && echo same"]
assert (trim diff.out) == "same" else "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: Monocypher and Rye tags disagree — Monocypher:\n$(cat ${cout})\nRye:\n$(cat ${rout})"

# 5. Anchor to the world: the eighth tag is RFC 8439 §2.5.2's published authenticator.
let rfc_tag = "a8061dc1305136c6c22b8baf0c0127a9"
let got_anchor = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '8p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_anchor.out) == rfc_tag else "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: the RFC 8439 §2.5.2 canonical tag is not the published a8061dc1305136c6c22b8baf0c0127a9"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${cout}"]
say "crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: the eight tags, agreed by both implementations:\n${shown.out}"

say "GREEN crypto-monocypher-poly1305-parity: our authored crypto/poly1305.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C, each compiled fresh, produce byte-for-byte identical Poly1305 authenticators over the block-edge sizes {0, 1, 15, 16, 17, 34, 256} and the RFC 8439 §2.5.2 canonical message (anchored to the published tag a8061dc1305136c6c22b8baf0c0127a9). The EIGHTH real Monocypher-SOURCE parity rung, closing the held horizon crypto/poly1305.rye itself named and proving the standalone MAC every Vault/Comlink/Lotus sealed carry rests on — no recited constant, the block-edge oracle a second real implementation. Monocypher stays vendored and unmodified, linked never copied. Purely local, no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."
